    "text": "To determine the total number of days John spent protesting, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Identify the number of days John attended the first protest.\n2. Calculate the number of days he attended the second protest, which is 25% longer than the first protest.\n3. Add the number of days from both protests to get the total number of days spent protesting.\n\nStep 1: The number of days John attended the first protest is 4 days.\n\nStep 2: The number of days he attended the second protest is 25% longer than the first protest. To find 25% of 4 days, we calculate:\n\\[ 25\\% \\text{ of } 4 = 0.25 \\times 4 = 1 \\text{ day} \\]\nSo, the second protest lasted:\n\\[ 4 + 1 = 5 \\text{ days} \\]\n\nStep 3: The total number of days John spent protesting is the sum of the days from both protests:\n\\[ 4 + 5 = 9 \\text{ days} \\]\n\nTherefore, the total number of days John spent protesting is \\(\\boxed{9}\\).",
